AUTO-DISCHARGE DOUBLE-FREE (off-board): GLM's emitter fix lets this nested/carried
label-fold COMPILE and re-invoke correctly (was the "never mutated" codegen bug).
But it now exposes a separate auto-discharge bug — carrying an obligation through a
loop (consume-in/issue-out) makes auto-discharge dispose the SEED binding h0 AND
escape the re-issued handle r (=h0) to the caller, which disposes again =>
double-free (calls destroy on h0 twice). The harness masks it (output still
matches, no hard crash). Off-board until auto-discharge credits the loop-carried
seed as consumed. See /tmp/nested-fold-codegen-brief.md.
